# Lint-clean workflow

Cursor Problems panel must stay red-free. This project enforces `eslint-plugin-react-hooks` v6 (purity, set-state-in-effect) — stricter than classic rules.

## Before finishing any edit session

```bash
pnpm run lint    # eslint . — must exit 0
pnpm run build   # tsc -b && vite build — must exit 0
```

Both run in CI-equivalent strictness. A change is not "done" while either fails.

## React purity rules (react-hooks/purity)

Never call impure functions (`Date.now()`, `Math.random()`, `crypto.randomUUID()`) during render — including JSX props and default values:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — impure call in render
<RateLimitModal blockedUntil={rateLimitedUntil ?? Date.now()} />

// ✅ GOOD — narrow the type so the fallback is unnecessary
{isRateLimited && rateLimitedUntil !== null ? (
  <RateLimitModal blockedUntil={rateLimitedUntil} />
) : null}
```

Allowed locations: event handlers, effect bodies, **lazy state initializers**:

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — lazy initializer
const [remaining, setRemaining] = useState(() => blockedUntil - Date.now());
```

## setState in effects (react-hooks/set-state-in-effect)

Don't call `setState` synchronously in an effect body. Compute initial state via lazy `useState(() => …)`; only update state inside timers/subscriptions/callbacks within the effect.

## Refs in effect cleanup (react-hooks/exhaustive-deps)

Copy `ref.current` to a local variable inside the effect before using it in cleanup:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const container = containerRef.current;
  // …
  return () => { container.innerHTML = ''; };
}, []);
```

## Generated files

`worker-configuration.d.ts` is generated by `wrangler types` — already in eslint `ignores`. Never hand-edit or lint-fix it.
